Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||12:19 AM||||Anybody know approx how much machine shops charge to balance a motor?  What other things should I consider having done to it?  Thanks in advance...||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||07-10-2000||09:37 AM||||Knife egde the crank! ($400)<BR>cryo align the rods and crank<BR>($138) <BR>Ferrea valves ($319)<P>the look on the Moostang owners face when he get TOASTED...<P>Priceless...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <P>but knife edging the crank makes a huge difference in the car ability to tack up and has less windage for better oiling. Coat the inside of the block with Glyptal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||02:28 PM||||Hey, good to see you back.  I've heard of knife-edging before and it sounds interesting... 400 bucks though!  You've gotta email me about you progress with the GT!||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||07-10-2000||04:34 PM||||GTB, I'm having my engine rebuilt, this is what's included:<P>tear down,<BR>hot tank,<BR>cylinder bored/honed,<BR>line aligned,<BR>new bearings, freeze plugs, seals, gaskets,<BR>pistons (rod/piston press)<BR>balance everything,<BR>valve job,<BR>put it back together.<P>I'm sure I've left out a few little things, basically it's everything that can be done short of blueprinting. and the quote I got was $900-$1400, $1400 being ultimate worst case senerio. But then I was wondering why I would spend that much on a 2.8, so I decided heck, throw in a 3.1 crank shaft for another $200, so, I'll probrably pay about $1100-$1500 all together. That's just a bit under the cost of the 3.4 crate engine, but if you get the 3.4 and put it in a fiero, you have to do extra mounting work (albeit not too much) and you also void the warrenty. so 3.1 w/ 3 year warrenty, or 3.4 no warrenty for a few extra hunderd?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||05:08 PM||||Thanks for the info Rick!  I've already done the teardown of the 2.8 I'm using.  All the assembly will be done by myself and a mechanic friend at his shop. All told, it'll cost me about 700 bucks.  I'm leaving the heads alone since 1FST2M6 had SI valves and new seals installed pretty recently.  Not sure about springs, but I might replace the seals again anyhow.  Possibly milling the heads a bit to make up the compression loss from going to dished hyper pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||07-10-2000||05:19 PM||||About $200-250 to balance the bottom end in New England.||||reg||1
